.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt VIPW 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm vipw
.Nd edit the account database
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility edits
.Pa /etc/master.passwd
by hand, safely.
It takes the database lock (the one
.Xr pw 8
takes), copies the file to
.Pa /etc/ptmp
with mode 0600, and runs an editor on the copy.
If the copy changed, it is checked as
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8
checks it and installed with
.Pa /etc/passwd
generated from it, as
.Ql pwd_mkdb -p
does.
If it does not check out, the problem is shown and
.Nm
asks whether to edit it again; otherwise nothing is installed.
Comment lines are not kept.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-d directory"
.It Fl d Ar directory
Edit and install the database in
.Ar directory
instead of
.Pa /etc .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width EDITOR
.It Ev EDITOR
The editor, with any arguments it needs; by default
.Pa /bin/vi .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/master.passwd -compact
.It Pa /etc/master.passwd
the account database
.It Pa /etc/passwd
its public form
.It Pa /etc/ptmp
the copy being edited
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr vi 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Bx 4.0 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
